<mxCell id="c69" value="Append a new REVERSAL/PAYOUT_REJECT_REFUND entry and preserve the original row and business reference." style="html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=15;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;align=left;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="2149" width="1790" height="50" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c70" value="Example: 2,000,000 gross -&gt; 200,000 tax and 1,800,000 net. There is no separate TAX_WITHHOLD ledger entry or 2,200,000 wallet debit. The threshold is per payout, not cumulative per month.&#xa;Mutation triggers run on UPDATE/DELETE/TRUNCATE, not each INSERT. A DBA/superuser can administer DDL; the diagram describes ordinary application/database constraints, not protection against all DBA actions.&#xa;Tax follows the project requirement. A snapshot is not proof that tax was remitted or that every legal tax scenario is supported." style="html=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=16;fontColor=#000000;strokeColor=#000000;fontSize=15;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#000000;align=left;spacing=12;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="2305" width="1830" height="100" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
